{"kind":"artifact","text":"The dissent section at internal/statusview on exact head b3b47533cfdd6e414bd1462ce21d41f15aaa0861. gs status renders a dissent, which carries no lifecycle and satisfies nothing, so it belonged to none of the five existing sections and was invisible on the page that is supposed to say what is disputed.\n\nThis replaces a30c9d84, which named the same path and the same commit and is unmergeable. I staled it myself: a30c9d84 rested on 93da3324, and I retired 93da3324's own basis 65f7efdd while clearing succession debt at docs. Staleness propagates through a stale basis, not only a retired one, so the retirement reached two hops down into a candidate for a head already under review, and gs merge refuses a stale artifact.\n\nThis one rests on request 5e951e50, the motivating request, and on nothing else. A request is not retired by merge succession, so no future merge at any path can reach this record. Anchoring a candidate to the predecessor artifact at its path is what put the previous pair in this state.","body":{"commit":"b3b47533cfdd6e414bd1462ce21d41f15aaa0861","path":"internal/statusview"}}